Modifications in this distribution
---------------------------------

- Restrict each task to an explicitly configured instance ID.
- Gate start, waiting, refresh and connect actions by the observed instance state.
- Use an elapsed-time deadline when waiting for an instance to become ready.
- Retry the complete per-account flow up to three times, with a five-second
  delay and a fresh status query before each attempt.
- Validate HTTP responses, business errors and required response fields.
- Request instance/refresh before obtaining a connection ticket.
- Report successful refresh/ticket requests without claiming permanent uptime.
- Reuse Qinglong's sendNotify module and notify only on final workflow failure
  or a configuration/startup failure; successful checks and wakeups are silent.
- Add a runner that loads a private credentials file and isolates proxy
  environment variables within the task process.
- Add offline VM-based tests and deployment documentation.

Refresh endpoint provenance
---------------------------

The instance/refresh request was implemented from the official TeleAgent web
application's file-access flow. Its successful response is not evidence of a
permanent desktop session or a guarantee against platform sleep/shutdown.

The public ihpdc/teleagent-baohuo repository was inspected as a feature and API
reference:

https://github.com/ihpdc/teleagent-baohuo

The console modules in this repository were implemented independently. No
source code from that repository is included. Its repository page did not
declare a license when inspected; this notice does not grant or imply any
license to its code.

